        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "1507d36d-1bf2-5544-a1c3-999f986ab3fa",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: HNoMS Draug\n- Organizations: Royal Norwegian Navy\n- Concepts: Draugr, Norse mythology\n\nFacts:\n- Two ships of the Royal Norwegian Navy have borne the name HNoMS \"Draug\".\n- HNoMS \"Draug\" was named after the sea revenant Draugr.\n- The draugr, also called draug or aptrganga/aptrgangr, is an undead creature from Norse mythology.\n- The term aptrganga or aptrgangr literally means \"again-walker\".\n- The draugr is called \"draugr\" in Old Norse, \"draugur\" in modern Icelandic, \"dreygur\" in Faroese, and \"draug\" in Danish, Swedish, and Norwegian.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
